    title: "Redeeming Your Time",
    scripture: "Ephesians 5:15-16",
    verse: "Be very careful, then, how you live—not as unwise but as wise, making the most of every opportunity, because the days are evil.",
    reflection: "Time is your most valuable resource. You can earn more money, but you can't get more time. Every day is 24 hours - how are you spending them? Scrolling endlessly? Binge-watching shows? Procrastinating? Or investing in what matters? Wise people redeem time. They prioritize relationships over entertainment, growth over comfort, eternal impact over temporary pleasure. This doesn't mean no rest or fun - God designed you for both. But it means being intentional. Track your time for one week. You'll be shocked where hours go. Then realign. What needs more time? What needs less? Make the most of every opportunity - not through frantic busyness, but through purposeful living. Today, identify one time-waster you can eliminate. Redirect that time toward something that matters. Redeem your time.",
